Ian Jackson
    Author of with-lock-ex.c, the C program whose locking strategy and
    usage semantics inspired withlock's design. Placed in the public
    domain by him.

Martin Caj and Martin Vidner (SUSE)
    Noticed that the got_lock variable was not declared global, which
    left the lock file behind after otherwise successful runs (0.4).

Jan Beran (Red Hat)
    Modernised the script for Python 2 and Python 3 compatibility
    (release 0.5).

Bernhard M. Wiedemann (SUSE)
    Found the test case that exposed the lock file cleanup bug, where a
    file was removed even when no lock had been obtained, and provided
    the fix (boo#864785). Also contributed the patch that re-opens the
    lock file before every locking attempt, which is part of the sources
    since 0.6.

rool.dev 
    Helped me with the footwork of releasing 0.6. 

